# Jira Agent Operating Rules (cursor-mathmodel)

## Agent identity (THIS repo only)

```yaml
AGENT_ID: cursor-mathmodel
AGENT_ROLE: mathmodel
TECHNOLOGIES:
  - Python
  - FastAPI
  - TypeScript
  - React
  - Level2 HTTP/WS client (read-only)
```

- Do **not** pretend to be the Level2 platform agent.
- **Never** modify `github.com/popelev/level2` or `~/level2` (no clone/edit/commit/push/PR/SSH changes there).
- For Level2 platform work: **create/update Jira only** with a clear English contract for another agent.

## Language

- Code, UI labels, README, comments, OpenAPI, Jira description bodies: **English**
- Chat with humans: Russian OK

## Jira is source of truth

- Task ownership and status live in Jira (project SCRUM, cloud `popelevfedor.atlassian.net`).
- Only work issues where **Assignee is you** OR ownership label **`ai-agent-cursor-mathmodel`** is set
  (as of 2026-08-10 there is **no** custom field named "AI Agent" on SCRUM Tasks — use labels until one exists).
- Prefer picking work in status mapped as **AI Ready**. If already **In Progress** (`В работе`), verify ownership before continuing.
- Never take another agent's task.

### Discovered SCRUM workflow mapping (2026-08-10)

| Agent rule name | Actual Jira status | Transition name |
|-----------------|--------------------|-----------------|
| AI Ready | `К выполнению` | `К выполнению` |
| In Progress | `В работе` | `В работе` |
| AI Review | `Тестирование` | `Testing` |
| Done | `Готово` | `Готово` |

Also present: `Idea`. Ownership labels: `ai-agent-cursor-mathmodel`, `ai-agent-level2`.

## Workflow

### On start (owned / AI Ready issue)

1. Transition **AI Ready → In Progress** (or equivalent available transition).
2. Comment:

```text
Started by: cursor-mathmodel
Plan: <short plan>
Expected changes: <files/areas>
```

### While working

- Commits must include issue key: `SCRUM-XXX ...`
- Prefer branch: `SCRUM-XXX-short-description`
- Keep Jira comments short; do not dump huge code into Jira.

### On finish

1. Comment in **Completed** format (what shipped, tests, commit hashes, blockers).
2. Transition **In Progress → AI Review** (or **Done** only if workflow requires it and work is verified).

## Boundaries for mathmodel

- Read-only Level2 client (`LEVEL2_API_URL`). No Level2 write/PUT.
- Imported tags → catalog + bindings; model/plan outputs → local vars only.
- Bind by stable `tag_id` (+ `device_id`).
- Do not disrupt level2-collector / Jenkins on the lab VM.

## Platform asks

When Level2 must change: file a SCRUM Task under epic **SCRUM-5**, prefix `[Mathmodel]`, relate to **SCRUM-17** / **SCRUM-20**, mark **Intended implementer: Level2 platform agent (not mathmodel)**. Set AI Agent to the Level2 agent id if known; otherwise leave unassigned with that note.
